CORE
main.cpp
--cpp17
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ g1 and g2 destroyed during unwinding: SUCCESS$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
[except.ctor]/1-3 -- objects constructed between try entry and a throwing call
(g1) and locals of intermediate functions without a try (g2) are destroyed
during unwinding.  Fixed by guarded call-site unwind cleanups: after each
possibly-throwing call the goto conversion emits destructors of the objects
between the call's scope and the innermost enclosing try (construction-state
aware) followed by a propagate-marker dispatch.  Cross-checked against g++ and
clang++.
